& [RefinementSubject] is one versioned temporal-semantic walk
  + [source_impulse] is Cantor centrally plans time, preserves the path walked, reflects backward over change, and joins that reflection with forward work
  + [refined_center] is Planner projects candidate paths, Calendar records authorized temporal commitments and wake conditions, SemanticRepository preserves material events, ChangeCapsule binds intent to actual change and review, and Observer alone admits the next generation
  + [compiler_correspondence] is forward construction followed by rear source, semantic, impact, target, and proof review under the signed SMTC language purpose
  + [canonical_authority] is absent_until_CTPR-SJS-01

& [StableTermMap_PlanningAndTime] is exact
  + [Planner] is the faculty and service contract that projects and revises candidate objective paths through dependencies, time, resources, effects, review, uncertainty, verification, stop, and reroute
  + [Calendar] is a versioned local temporal projection of proposals, tentative holds, authorized commitments, availability, deadlines, recurrences, wake conditions, review points, misses, cancellations, and completion
  + [PlanRevision] is one immutable candidate path generation with objectives, dependencies, estimates, alternatives, effects, review gates, schedule projections, and uncertainty
  + [Schedule] is a candidate allocation of work and review through time
  + [Commitment] is an authorized accepted temporal obligation under an eligible principal and exact scope
  + [CalendarItem] is one stable item identity with immutable revisions and explicit lifecycle
  + [WakeCondition] is a reentry trigger that first causes current-state revalidation and never directly authorizes work
  + [TimeExpression] binds time domain, value or interval, source, timezone, precision, interpretation policy, and uncertainty
  + [civil_time] is human calendar representation under named zone and calendar rules
  + [instant_time] is a UTC-relative point under declared conversion rules
  + [monotonic_time] is process-relative elapsed ordering without civil meaning
  + [logical_time] is deterministic fixture or causal progression time
  + [valid_time] is when an assertion applies to its subject
  + [transaction_time] is when Cantor records a revision
  + [uncertain_time] is interval, estimate, partial date, or unresolved zone

& [StableTermMap_RepositoryAndChange] is exact
  + [SemanticRepository] is an append-only material-event journal plus immutable content store, predecessor-bound snapshot DAG, reference indexes, and declared projections
  + [RepositoryGeneration] is one immutable policy, predecessor frontier, and admitted event frontier
  + [MaterialEvent] is one materially observable semantic, task, tool, effect, review, calendar, fault, admission, or reentry boundary
  + [MicroEvent] is a non-material high-frequency observation retained only under explicit liveness, debugging, fault, or analysis policy
  + [ContentObject] is immutable payload bytes plus digest and provenance
  + [SemanticSnapshot] is a materialized semantic state derived from exact predecessor snapshots and an admitted event frontier
  + [GitProjection] is a human-facing file, diff, commit, branch, tag, or note view of selected repository material and is not the sole repository authority
  + [CaptureCadence] is a materiality and retention policy rather than a literal record per token or wall-clock tick
  + [ChangeCapsule] is the typed waist binding prior intent, before state, candidate work, observed change, distinct diff surfaces, rear review, invalidation, Observer disposition, and admitted after state

& [StableTermMap_LanesAndJoin] is exact
  + [ProspectiveLane] reads one admitted version and prepares a bounded candidate or next work packet
  + [ExecutionLane] performs only separately authorized operations against one pinned version and returns observed outcomes
  + [RetrospectiveLane] reviews one exact prior transition against its declared intent, evidence, contracts, effects, and resulting meaning
  + [LaneCursor] binds lane, task, input generation, plan revision, capsule generation, dependencies, lease, timeout, and authority scope
  + [PreparedAhead] means draft, retrieve, simulate, compile, or stage without admitting a dependent transition or committing an effect
  + [ReflectionReturn] is one version-bound rear disposition with evidence, objections, uncertainty, invalidation mask, and residual
  + [ObserverJoin] is the only reconciliation that may admit, qualify, repair, branch, revert, compensate, block, or preserve unresolved state
  + [ReleaseBarrier] blocks dependent admission and effects until applicable rear review or an explicit bounded-lag policy is satisfied
  + [CompareAndAppend] means the join succeeds only when expected predecessor, generation, dependency, and authority conditions remain current

& [StableTermMap_DiffsAndCompiler] is exact
  + [PhysicalDiff] is byte, file, database-row, graph-record, package, or external-resource change
  + [SourceDiff] is source artifact and source-span change
  + [SemanticDiff] is identity, context, relation, type, contract, state, authority, uncertainty, or lifecycle meaning change
  + [BuildDiff] is dependency, compiler, SemanticIR, index, artifact, package, or invalidation change
  + [BehavioralDiff] is change in observable evaluation or interaction
  + [EffectDiff] is proposed, authorized, committed, failed, compensated, or observed external-state change
  + [ProofDiff] is requirement, fixture, evidence, diagnostic, support, or confidence change
  + [CalendarDiff] is estimate, schedule, commitment, trigger, delay, miss, recurrence, or completion change
  + [CompilerWalk] is forward parse, resolve, lower, and project followed by rear source, semantic, impact, correspondence, and proof review before package admission
  + [CompilerGeneration] binds source, dependencies, profile, compiler, SemanticIR, targets, correspondence, loss, diagnostics, and proof generations

& [StableTermMap_Learning] is exact
  + [ForecastError] compares preserved estimate with actual observed duration, cost, risk, effects, and completion evidence
  + [PlanDeviation] records skipped, inserted, reordered, blocked, repeated, or abandoned steps without rewriting the original plan
  + [SemanticSurprise] records a meaning, dependency, identity, or boundary exposed by actual work
  + [LessonCandidate] is a reviewed proposal for future planning or SOP change and has no durable learning authority yet
  + [TrainingExampleCandidate] is a sensitivity-reviewed projection of intent, change, disposition, and next-plan quality and is not admitted corpus data by default

& [RejectedConflationSet] is binding
  + Planner is not Calendar
  + plan is not schedule
  + schedule is not commitment
  + deadline or proximity is not priority or authority
  + wake is not permission to execute
  + notification is not effect authorization
  + timestamp is not sufficient causal order
  + record order is not necessarily valid time
  + every_moment is not every token, thought, clock tick, filesystem notification, or insignificant event
  + sequential snapshot is not atomic world state
  + SemanticRepository is not merely Git
  + Git commit is not necessarily one semantic transition
  + textual diff is not semantic diff
  + semantic diff is not automatically behavioral or effect diff
  + observed correlation is not causation
  + rear reflection is not retrospective rationalization
  + prepared candidate is not admitted successor
  + lane concurrency is not shared mutable semantic or hidden attention state
  + model narration is not lane completion proof
  + ReflectionReturn is not Observer disposition
  + accepted review is not effect authority
  + LessonCandidate is not adopted routine
  + TrainingExampleCandidate is not authorized corpus
  + compiler output is not independent correspondence proof
  + generated package is not admitted package

& [FacultyIntegration] preserves responsibility
  + Observer owns cycle opening, lane routing, return reconciliation, final disposition, and continuation
  + Honesty checks time facts, identities, forecasts, attributions, causal claims, diff meaning, evidence, and hindsight integrity
  + Security checks principal, authority, calendar privacy, participants, resources, disclosures, mutations, effects, retention, and provider boundaries
  + Scribe anchors before state and preserves plans, events, capsules, reviews, dispositions, after state, and reentry
  + Refiner minimizes the next admissible delta and detects semantic distortion
  + Weaver projects compatible identity, operation, resource, tool, participant, artifact, and target compositions
  + Planner projects reachable paths, schedules, alternatives, review points, fallback, stop, and reroute
  + faculties advise or gate according to their signed contracts; none independently admits the successor state

& [SMTCIntegration] uses signed language semantics
  + CTPR forms are definitions, data, contracts, profiles, tests, and explicit programs under document and region roles
  + CompilerWalk consumes one source-mapped SemanticIR and distinct target projections
  + rear correspondence cannot be performed solely by the target generator being checked
  + all effectful scheduling, calendar synchronization, Git mutation, notification, provider, and background work remains RuntimeABI and EffectBroker work
  + CTPR specification does not imply an implemented compiler

& [WalkingAttentionIntegrationCandidate] is behavior mapping pending fresh fidelity proof
  + forward continuity maps to ProspectiveLane framing and bounded next seed
  + rear reflection maps to RetrospectiveLane comparison and refusal power
  + tandem exchange maps to explicit versioned messages, acknowledgments, returns, joins, invalidation, and release
  + reentry maps to exact continuation state after disposition
  + hidden attention, private reasoning, literal simultaneous hidden-state sharing, unrestricted executor authority, and fixed pacing remain excluded

& [UncertaintyLedger] remains explicit
  + storage engine, serialization, indexes, compaction, and retention implementation are not selected
  + calendar provider, schedule solver, time library, notification adapter, and recurrence engine are not selected
  + lane concurrency may be sequential, threaded, process-isolated, machine-distributed, or model-mediated behind the same versioned protocol
  + materiality thresholds require profile and empirical tuning
  + semantic diff precision and independent compiler correspondence require later implementation proof
  + learned planning or rear-review models may provide no measurable benefit and must preserve deterministic fallback
  + ECS is a promising runtime projection for identity-component separation, system queries, scheduling, and command buffering but is not selected as the canonical ontology or storage model

& [IntegratedExpression] is the stable core
  + Cantor advances through immutable ChangeCapsules: Planner prepares a candidate path, Calendar binds authorized temporal commitments and wake conditions, Scribe records material events, execution operates against a pinned generation, rear review compares declared intent with distinct actual deltas, and Observer admits or rejects the next version before dependent release
  + the compiler follows the same bidirectional shape over one signed SemanticIR and proof-carrying target family

& [RefinementCheck] completes WS-CTPR-005
  + [identity_preserved] is true
  + [source_overwrite] is false
  + [uncertainty_preserved] is true
  + [rejected_conflation_count] is 24
  + [remaining_semantic_collision] is none blocking conceptual data design
  + [support_delta] is FR-CTPR-005 ready_for_verification
  + [next_workers] are WS-CTPR-006 formal data design and WS-CTPR-007 Walking Attention fidelity revalidation
  + [canonical_authority] is absent_until_CTPR-SJS-01
